+				<p>“Some English girls and boys are coming to see me tomorrow and I want to have a jolly time. If it’s fine, I’m going to pitch my tent in Longmeadow, and row up the whole crew to lunch and croquet⁠—have a fire, make messes, gypsy fashion, and all sorts of larks. They are nice people, and like such things. Brooke will go, to keep us boys steady, and <span epub:type="z3998:personal-name">Kate Vaughn</span> will play propriety for the girls. I want you all to come; can’t let Beth off, at any price, and nobody shall worry her. Don’t bother about rations⁠—I’ll see to that, and everything else⁠—only do come, there’s a good fellow!</p>
 				<p epub:type="z3998:valediction">“In a tearing hurry,</p>
 				<p epub:type="z3998:valediction">“Yours ever,</p>
 				<p epub:type="z3998:signature">“Laurie.”</p>
